AI Stock Analyzer Pro - README

Note you can go to: ist495-trader-agent-production-a87c.up.railway.app for the public website.

⚡ Quick Start Guide
Requirements
Python 3.11.9 (exact version required)

Internet connection for API calls

2GB RAM minimum

One-Click Setup
bash
# 1. Clone or download the repository
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd ai-stock-analyzer

# 2. Create and activate virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

# 3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 4. Create .env file (see below)
# 5. Run the app
python app.py
Open http://localhost:5000 in your browser.

📁 Project Structure
text
ai-stock-analyzer/
├── app.py              # Main application (all code)
├── .env                # API keys (create this)
├── .env.example        # Template for API keys
├── requirements.txt    # Python dependencies
├── runtime.txt         # Python version
├── Procfile           # Railway deployment
├── start.sh           # Startup script
└── README.md          # This file
🔑 Required API Keys
Create a .env file with:

env
# REQUIRED - Get from https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_key

# REQUIRED - Get from https://www.alphavantage.co/support/#api-key
ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY=your_alpha_vantage_key

# OPTIONAL - For additional AI providers
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_key
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_key
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key

# Generate with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
SECRET_KEY=your_secret_key
Minimum Viable Setup: Only Gemini and Alpha Vantage keys are required. The app will run with just these two.

🚀 Running the Application
Local Development
bash
python app.py
# App runs on http://localhost:5000
Production (Gunicorn)
bash
gunicorn --worker-tmp-dir /dev/shm app:app
Railway Deployment
bash
railway up
🛠️ What the App Does
Feature	Description
Stock Analysis	Analyzes 200+ stocks with AI recommendations
AI Integration	Supports Gemini, OpenAI, Claude, Groq
News Scraping	Aggregates news from 5 sources
Paper Trading	Virtual trading with $10,000 starting balance
Predictions	ML-based price predictions
Technical Indicators	RSI, MACD, ADX, Bollinger Bands
📡 Key Endpoints
Endpoint	Method	Purpose
/	GET	Web interface
/api/analyze	POST	Analyze stocks
/api/paper/status	GET	Portfolio status
/api/paper/buy	POST	Buy shares
/api/paper/sell	POST	Sell shares
/api/paper/reset	POST	Reset account
/api/export	POST	Export CSV data
/api/status	GET	App status
🔧 Troubleshooting
Issue	Solution
Module not found	pip install -r requirements.txt
Port in use	Change port in app.py or kill process
API key errors	Check .env file exists and keys are valid
Database errors	Ensure write permissions in current directory
News not loading	Wait 2-3 minutes for cache refresh
Common Commands
bash
# Check Python version
python --version  # Must be 3.11.9

# Install specific package
pip install flask==2.3.3

# Kill process on port 5000 (Linux/macOS)
lsof -ti:5000 | xargs kill -9

# Kill process on port 5000 (Windows)
netstat -ano | findstr :5000
taskkill /PID <PID> /F
📊 Testing Your Installation
bash
# Start the app
python app.py

# In another terminal, test the API
curl http://localhost:5000/api/status
Expected response shows "status":"online" and AI availability status.

🚨 Important Notes
Python Version: Must be exactly 3.11.9 (specified in runtime.txt)

.env File: Must be in the root directory

Internet Required: For stock data and AI calls

AI Fallbacks: App works with technical analysis if AI keys are missing

